        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="234" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>Content that knows what it is</header>
                <paragraph>In Exponential every piece of content belongs to a content class: an article has a title, an intro, a body and an image; an event has a start and an end; a product has a price. Editors fill in fields, not page layouts, so the same content can appear as a card on the home page, a full page, an RSS item or a JSON response without being written twice.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>Classes you design</header>
                <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">More than forty field types, from rich text and images to prices, map locations, keywords and relations.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Required fields, validation and translatable fields per class.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Object relations that keep links between content intact when things move.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>One tree, many views</header>
                <paragraph>Each object has a place in the content tree and can appear in several places at once. Templates choose the view mode (full, line, embed, block item), so a design change never touches the content.</paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
